


The estream_puts Function "estream_puts.h"

            The estream_puts function takes no action if #0
            is a null pointer or if #0 specifies a null
            string. Otherwise, the estream_put_phrase
            function function indirectly writes to the
            standard error stream the initial non-null
            characters of the string pointed to by #0.
              If there is not enough room on the current
            line to write each of the initial characters, a
            soft line break is inserted before writing the
            characters specified by #0.
              The number of characters written is limited to
            HSTR_LEN_MAX.
              Characters are sent to the standard error
            stream via estream_put_hstr with the requisite
            transformations.
              The caller must guarantee that #0 indicates an
            object whose initial HSTR_SIZE_MAX characters
            are accessible or that contains a null character
            within HSTR_SIZE_MAX characters.
